      "summary": "The trace processor replaces sensitive values but keeps their names. A prompt tag or event attribute therefore remains in exported telemetry, violating AC-03.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/DiagnosticsSetup.cs",
          "line": 119,
          "message": "Sensitive span and event attribute names are retained after redaction, contrary to AC-03.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "RedactingActivityProcessor.OnEnd calls TryRedact for span tags and event attributes. For sensitive names, TryRedact returns the redacted placeholder, and the processor writes it back under the original key.",
            "failureScenario": "When an activity has a span tag or event attribute named prompt, the exporter receives that name with value [redacted]. AC-03 requires sensitive names as well as values to be absent from captured tags and event attributes."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
      "reviewType": "testing",
      "harness": "codex",
      "harnessVersion": "0.162.0",
      "model": "gpt-6-luna",
      "approved": false,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 2,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The logging processor can export interpolated free text when an exception is attached. The trace test also does not verify AC-03’s requirement that sensitive names be absent.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/DiagnosticsSetup.cs",
          "line": 99,
          "message": "An exception makes the formatted-message guard ineffective for messages without structured placeholders. Omit the body or otherwise prevent interpolated free text from reaching the exporter.",
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "RedactingLogProcessor.OnEnd adds exception.type to source before checking source.Count, then renders data.Body from the redacted attributes.",
            "failureScenario": "When a caller logs an exception with an interpolated message containing a credential, such as logger.LogError(exception, \"Authorization: \" + token), exception.type makes source nonempty. RenderMessage receives a body with no placeholders and returns it unchanged, so the credential can reach the exporter. This violates AC-05. OWASP A09:2025."
          }
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/DiagnosticsTests.cs",
          "line": 301,
          "message": "AC-03 requires the trace tests to assert that sensitive names are absent from span tags and event attributes; the current test checks values only, so that behavior can regress without failing the test.",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The trace pipeline test asserts that sensitive values are absent from captured span tags and event tags, but does not assert that sensitive tag names are absent.",
            "failureScenario": "If the processor retains a sensitive name such as prompt with a replacement value, the current value-only assertions still pass, although AC-03 requires sensitive names to be absent."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
